# Organic Promotion (SEO) — Infrastructure Rules

## Technical foundation (every public project, from the skeleton stage)
- `app/sitemap.ts` — dynamic sitemap of all indexable URLs (pages, articles, landing pages) with `lastModified`;
  split into a sitemap index when > 50,000 URLs. Excludes admin, auth, thank-you, filtered/duplicate URLs.
- `app/robots.ts` — production: allow site, disallow `/admin`, `/api`, private paths, link to sitemap.
  development/staging: `Disallow: /` **and** `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` header.
- Metadata API on every page: unique `title` (≤ 60 chars) and `description` (≤ 155), `alternates.canonical`,
  Open Graph + Twitter cards, OG image (`opengraph-image.tsx`). `metadataBase` set per environment.
- Structured data (JSON-LD): `Organization`/`LocalBusiness` (site-wide), `WebSite` + `SearchAction`, `BreadcrumbList`,
  `Article`/`BlogPosting` (articles), `FAQPage` where real FAQs exist, `Product`/`Service`/`SoftwareApplication` as relevant.
  Validated with Google's Rich Results Test before launch.
- Clean, readable URLs (Hebrew slugs transliterated or English, decided per project, consistent), one H1 per page,
  logical heading hierarchy, descriptive internal anchor text, breadcrumbs.
- `hreflang` + `lang`/`dir` when bilingual. 301 redirects map when replacing an existing site (never lose old URLs).
- Images: `next/image`, descriptive file names, `alt`, modern formats, explicit sizes.

## "High rate on Google" = measurable quality targets
- Lighthouse (mobile) ≥ 90 for Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices and SEO on key pages — enforced in CI (Lighthouse CI).
- Core Web Vitals "Good" in field data: LCP < 2.5s, INP < 200ms, CLS < 0.1.
- Zero crawl errors, valid sitemap, all key pages indexed in Google Search Console.
- For paid traffic: landing page relevance and speed to support a high Google Ads Quality Score (see `14-paid-marketing`).

## Measurement & pixels readiness (prepared in code, activated per environment)
- Google Search Console (domain property, DNS verification) + sitemap submitted; Bing Webmaster Tools.
- GA4 (via GTM or `@next/third-parties`), with conversion events: `generate_lead`, `contact`, `sign_up`, `purchase`.
- Meta Pixel + Conversions API, Google Ads conversion tag + enhanced conversions, TikTok/LinkedIn pixels when used.
- All IDs from env vars; a single `lib/analytics` module emits events to all destinations with shared `event_id`.
- Consent banner where required; tracking respects consent. Pixels disabled/test-mode outside production.

## Content at scale (target: 1,000+ keyword-driven articles per site, built over time)
- Start from keyword research → topic clusters (pillar page + cluster articles) → keyword map
  (`docs/marketing/keyword-map.csv`: keyword, intent, volume, difficulty, cluster, target URL, status).
- One primary keyword + search intent per article; no two articles targeting the same intent (avoid cannibalization).
- Articles stored as MDX in `content/` or in the DB/CMS with: title, slug, meta, author, dates, cluster, internal links, schema.
- **Quality gate for every article** (Google penalizes mass-produced low-value content — "scaled content abuse"):
  original value, factual accuracy checked, real author/expert byline (E-E-A-T), Hebrew proofread, internal links to
  pillar + 2–5 related articles, no AI text published without human review.
- Publishing cadence planned (e.g. batches per week), indexing monitored in Search Console; refresh decaying articles.
- Programmatic pages (location × service etc.) only when each page has genuinely unique, useful data.
Implementation: skills `site-architecture`, `seo-foundation`, `content-engine`, `competitor-content-gap`, `gsc-ctr-optimizer` — orchestrated by `growth-engine`.

## Social / organic networks
- Every page shareable with proper OG; social profiles linked in `Organization.sameAs`.
- Content repurposing plan: each article → social posts/reels script/WhatsApp status/newsletter snippet.
